      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 896756924,
          "type": "DiffNote",
          "body": "This _probably_ would lead to a ReportedBoundsError, but someone might just have encoded it with a specification violating length of 127. Also see \"NOTE 2 – In the long form, it is a sender's option whether to use more length octets than the minimum necessary,\" from ITU-T X.690.\n\nI think it makes more sense to flag this as a separate BER specific expert info at the PI_WARN PI_PROTOCOL level, try to interpret it with the illegal value, and only throw the ReportedBoundsError if it happens naturally from running off the end.\n\nDistinguish between \"someone just didn't read 8.1.3.5 c) but it would be valid if 1111111 were acceptable\" and a really messed up packet.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
