        {
          "id": 896821773,
          "type": "DiffNote",
          "body": "`BER` calls them all errors but assigns a severity of `PI_WARN`.  \n\n```\n{ &ei_ber_expected_set, { \"ber.error.expected.set\", PI_MALFORMED, PI_WARN, \"BER Error: SET expected\", EXPFILL }},\n```\n\nCouchbase is close but gave it's one error a serverity of `PI_WARN`.  \n\n[Display Filter Reference: Couchbase Protocol](https://www.wireshark.org/docs/dfref/c/couchbase.html)  \n[packet-couchbase.c](https://gitlab.com/wireshark/wireshark/-/blob/master/epan/dissectors/packet-couchbase.c#L3863)  \n```\n{ &ef_illegal_value, { \"couchbase.warn.illegal_value\", PI_UNDECODED, PI_WARN, \"Illegal value for command\", EXPFILL }},\n{ &ef_compression_error, { \"couchbase.error.compression\", PI_UNDECODED, PI_WARN, \"Compression error\", EXPFILL }},\n```  \n\nOpenSafety matches the field name with the severity level.  \n  \n[Display Filter Reference: openSAFETY](https://www.wireshark.org/docs/dfref/o/opensafety.html)  \n[packet-opensafety.c](https://gitlab.com/wireshark/wireshark/-/blob/master/epan/dissectors/packet-opensafety.c#L2847)  \n```\n          { \"opensafety.crc.error.frame1_invalid\", PI_PROTOCOL, PI_ERROR,\n          { \"opensafety.crc.error.frame1_valid_frame2_invalid\", PI_PROTOCOL, PI_ERROR,\n          { \"opensafety.crc.warning.wrong_crc_for_spdo\", PI_PROTOCOL, PI_WARN,\n```\n\nWould it be appropriate to start a `ber.warn` or `ber.warning` branch of expert messages?  \nIn the spirit of using 127 bytes maybe `ber.warn.you_made_the_length_field_really_long_was_that_the_intent`?  \nOr maybe just `ber.warning.suspect_length`. There is an existing error message for invalid length:  \n```\n{ &ei_ber_error_length, { \"ber.error.length\", PI_MALFORMED, PI_WARN, \"BER Error: length is not valid\", EXPFILL }},\n```",
          "author": {
            "id": 6701257,
            "username": "chuckcraft",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Chuck Craft",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
