        {
          "id": 898992940,
          "type": "DiffNote",
          "body": "`try_get_ber_length()` is isolated from the tree and packet info.  \n```\nstatic int\ntry_get_ber_length(tvbuff_t *tvb, int offset, guint32 *length, gboolean *ind, gint nest_level) {\n```\nI'm not sure it's possible to add an expert info without something to tie it to.  \n\nIs it worth adding parameters (tree, pinfo) to `get_ber_length()` and `try_get_ber_length()` to add an expert info that looks like might be a flip of the coin depending on how the RFC is read?\n\n```\nint\nget_ber_length(tvbuff_t *tvb, int offset, guint32 *length, gboolean *ind)\n{\n    return try_get_ber_length(tvb, offset, length, ind, 1);\n}\n```",
