    {
      "id": "cf702d7ad907a93ffa75e5cc2f0945038cc630da",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 901770085,
          "type": null,
          "body": "@johnthacker `get_ber_length()` was added in a6ed2d49.\n```\n- extern int dissect_ber_length(packet_info *pinfo, proto_tree *tree, tvbuff_t *tvb, int offset, guint32 *length);\n+ extern int get_ber_length(tvbuff_t *tvb, int offset, guint32 *length, gboolean *ind);\n+ extern int dissect_ber_length(packet_info *pinfo, proto_tree *tree, tvbuff_t *tvb, int offset, guint32 *length, gboolean *ind);\n```\nIt was a rework of `dissect_ber_length()` but unfortunately didn't get the `pinfo` and `tree` parameters.  \n`get_ber_length()` is in 30 other dissector and `.cnf` files (other that `packet-ber.[ch]`)  \nTrying to get `pinfo` and/or `tree` in every call would be tough.  \nIs it ok to make the call `get_ber_length(NULL, NULL, ...)` everywhere except spots where `pinfo` or `tree` are available?  \n  \nExample in [packet-ldap.c](https://gitlab.com/wireshark/wireshark/-/blob/master/epan/dissectors/packet-ldap.c#L3253):  \n```\n    offset=dissect_ber_identifier(actx->pinfo, NULL, tvb, offset, &ber_class, &pc, &tag);\n    offset=dissect_ber_length(actx->pinfo, NULL, tvb, offset, &len, &ind);\n```",
          "author": {
            "id": 6701257,
            "username": "chuckcraft",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Chuck Craft",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/0809ffc6d9d98013a1895132bc055c622830b8a20bfa49328f53d5eb4a1206cb?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/chuckcraft"
          },
          "created_at": "2022-04-05T22:25:37.408Z",
          "updated_at": "2022-04-05T22:49:47.624Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 147209877,
